Directory & Contacts > How do I setup a new User and send email with Login credentials?

When you click that checkbox, you’ll be prompted to select a role, give a username, and give an email address. After you selected a role, you’ll see how much access that person gets once he logs in on the below field. But you’ll not be able to customize it there because roles need to be setup in the settings. Click here to see how to create new roles and modify existing roles. Once you select a role, enter a username and an email address, and click save, that person will get an email to setup his password and login to the account. If an employee leaves the company or no longer needs access to Contractor Foreman, you can easily deactivate their account by unchecking the Allow login access check box in their profile. This disables their login access without deleting their employee record, allowing you to retain any project history or data associated with their work. Further, once you allowed login access to a person, you’ll see a field on that person’s profile called Access Details”. Here you can setup the following;
You can set a default cost code for that person so when that person uses time cards, that cost code will be automatically selected.

